    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the structured address form for owner creation, keeping the flat `address` input backward-compatible.\n\n### Changes\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** (drives the generated DTOs)\n- Added `addressLine1` and optional `addressLine2` string properties to `OwnerFields`.\n- Removed `address` from the `required` list so a structured-only request passes bean validation at the API boundary (the either/or rule is now enforced in the controller). `firstName`, `lastName`, `city`, `telephone` stay required.\n- Documented `address` as the composed/returned value.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**\n- Added `addressLine1` / `addressLine2` fields (`@Column`) with getters/setters. MapStruct auto-maps them onto `OwnerDto`, so both are returned; and from `OwnerFieldsDto` on create.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 `resolveAddressFields`\n- Prefers structured fields: when `addressLine1` is non-blank, it and `addressLine2` are normalized in place and `address` is set to the composed value (`normalized addressLine1` + a single space + `normalized addressLine2` when line 2 is present).\n- Otherwise falls back to normalizing the flat `address`, exactly as before.\n- Validity/normalization/household-hash/postcode-validation/locality all read the resolved fields (`city`/`postcode` are structured and read directly; the composed `address` is what's stored and returned). Updated the `validateRequiredFields` Javadoc accordingly.\n\n**Schema + seed data** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`, `db/hsqldb/data.sql`)\n- Added `address_line1` / `address_line2` columns at the **end** of the `owners` table, and appended two `NULL`s to the hsqldb positional seed inserts (the other profiles use column-named inserts, so they needed no data changes).\n\nThe two acceptance tests \u2014 structured address normalized + composed, and flat address still accepted \u2014 both pass.",
